pagewire's change to PAPPL v1.4.12: close the web interface's admin pages
when no authentication service is set.

Upstream papplClientHTMLAuthorize() lets every client use the admin pages
when no auth service, auth callback or access password is set. That is how
the retrofit Printer Applications run in pagewire, and they listen on every
address of the node, so any LAN client could add, change or delete printers.

With this patch papplClientHTMLAuthorize() answers 403 Forbidden whenever no
auth service or callback is set; the access password is ignored. That closes
PAPPL's system and printer admin pages, the printer page's form actions
(pause, resume, hold, release, set as default, identify, print test page;
the patch adds the authorization check there, which upstream lacks), and the
application-added pages that call it, such as pappl-retrofit's /addppd (PPD
upload) and hplip-printer-app's /plugin (plugin download and install). The
status pages stay readable. IPP administration stays loopback-only, as
upstream has it.

